title: Edits in progress
tags: Commands [[Cross-panel selection]]
kind: reference
summary: Text a panel holds that nothing has saved stops the selection from moving unless you agree, and closing a workspace or the GUI asks first.

An ''edit in progress'' is a field being edited or added in the [[metarecord-detail panel]],
or a text file with unsaved changes in the [[viewer panel]] ([[Editing a text file]]).

|!What would lose it |!Asks |!If you refuse |
|moving the selection of its workspace |''Unsaved changes in … — discard them and move the selection?'' |the selection stays where it is, for every panel |
|`workspace:close`, a tab's close button |''Unsaved changes in … — discard them and close?'' |the workspace stays |
|`quit`, closing the window |the same, for every workspace |the GUI stays |

Writing the selection it already holds is no move, and asks nothing.

The cursor of a list that publishes the selection asks before moving, so a refusal
leaves it on its row: [[metarecord-list panel]], [[file-manager panel]], [[path-ref panel]],
[[recent panel]], [[duplicates panel]].

Going into another folder or node is not held back: the list changes, and only its
selection stays.

Scripts are not stopped by it. A selection written through `mf gui view`, or a workspace
closed from outside the GUI, does not ask first: the panels still keep their edit when
the selection moves that way, but closing loses it.

If the GUI's page hangs, the window cannot be closed from its title bar, since the page
is what answers: use the window manager's way of killing it.

!! For a panel

A panel declares its edit with `metafolder.provide`:

```
metafolder.provide({
  unsaved: () => (changed() ? 'notes.txt' : null), // named in the question
  discard: () => dropChanges(),                    // when the user agreed
});
```

A list asks before moving its cursor, with `mf.workspace.mayMoveSelection()`: true at once
when nothing is in progress, and an edit given up on a yes. ''The check is also'' in `workspace.set` and `workspace.setMany`, before the write, and a writer
setting `selected_metarecord` then `selected_paths` is asked once. The other selections
of the workspace (`workspace.send` from another one) go through without asking.
